      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    highs = [120, 122, 125, 123, 126, 124, 127, 129, 130, 128, 131, 133, 134, 135, 136, 137, 138, 139]\n    lows = [118, 120, 121, 119, 123, 122, 124, 126, 127, 126, 128, 130, 131, 132, 133, 134, 135, 136]\n    closes = [119, 121, 123, 120, 125, 123, 126, 128, 129, 127, 130, 132, 133, 134, 135, 136, 137, 138]\n    parameter_length = 14\n\n    true_ranges = []\n    vm_plus = []\n\n    for i in range(1, len(highs)):\n        true_range = max(\n            highs[i] - lows[i],\n            abs(highs[i] - closes[i - 1]),\n            abs(lows[i] - closes[i - 1])\n        )\n        true_ranges.append(true_range)\n        vm_plus.append(abs(highs[i] - lows[i - 1]))\n\n    # Calculate the last VI+ value\n    start = len(true_ranges) - parameter_length\n    sum_tr = sum(true_ranges[start:])\n    sum_vm_plus = sum(vm_plus[start:])\n    vi_plus = sum_vm_plus / sum_tr\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to four decimal places\n    return round(vi_plus, 4)\n```",
